{
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "exec": [
          "if (!pm.variables.get('baseUrl')) { pm.variables.set('baseUrl', 'http://localhost:8000'); }"
        ],
        "type": "text/javascript"
      }
    }
  ],
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "family-office-portal-collection",
    "description": "Private read-only family estate portal. The portal aggregates four backend services (llc-manager, pp-security-master, xero_crypto, family_office) behind a SQLite read-through cache and exposes five primary sections (home, documents, finances, portfolio, entities) plus an admin surface for refresh control. Page routes return server-rendered HTML; admin and health routes return JSON. See docs/planning/tech-spec.md for the full contract.",
    "name": "Family Office Portal API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "item": [
        {
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is in the expected range', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 422]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('response body is valid JSON', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody();",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "name": "Per-service refresh log",
          "request": {
            "description": "Return the most recent refresh outcome per backend service.\n\nAuthentication: Admin only via Cloudflare Access. Reads the ``refresh_log``\ntable populated by the APScheduler jobs.\n\nReturns:\n    RefreshStatusResponse: One entry per tracked backend.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "admin",
                "refresh-status"
              ],
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/refresh-status"
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is in the expected range', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([202, 422]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('response body is valid JSON', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody();",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "name": "Trigger a manual refresh",
          "request": {
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              },
              "raw": "{\n  \"force\": true\n}"
            },
            "description": "Enqueue an out-of-band refresh for the named backend service.\n\nAuthentication: Admin only via Cloudflare Access. Phase 0 returns a stub\nresponse; Phase 1 will dispatch to the APScheduler job for the matching\nservice (``entities``, ``holdings``, ``positions``, ``documents``).\n\nArgs:\n    service: Backend service identifier to refresh.\n    body: Trigger options; set ``force`` to bypass the staleness check.\n\nReturns:\n    RefreshTriggerResponse: Confirmation of the scheduling decision.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "admin",
                "refresh",
                ":service"
              ],
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/refresh/:service",
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "service",
                  "value": "example"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "name": "admin"
    },
    {
      "item": [
        {
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is in the expected range', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 422]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "name": "List document folders",
          "request": {
            "description": "Render the document folder view.\n\nAuthentication: Viewer or Admin via Cloudflare Access. Data is read from\nthe SQLite cache populated by the ``refresh_documents`` job; the route\nnever calls the upstream ``family_office`` service directly (ADR-003).\n\nReturns:\n    HTMLResponse: Placeholder folder listing page.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "documents"
              ],
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/documents"
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is in the expected range', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 422]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('response body is valid JSON', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.jsonBody();",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "name": "Search documents by name",
          "request": {
            "description": "Return documents whose name matches ``q``.\n\nAuthentication: Viewer or Admin via Cloudflare Access. Designed as an HTMX\npartial in Phase 1; the JSON shape is returned at Phase 0 so the contract\nis OpenAPI-described from the start.\n\nArgs:\n    q: Free-text query string; must be at least one character.\n\nReturns:\n    DocumentSearchResponse: Matching documents in ranked order.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "documents",
                "search"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "description": "Free-text search query.",
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "example"
                }
              ],
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/documents/search"
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is in the expected range', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 422]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "name": "Download original document",
          "request": {
            "description": "Stream the original document as a file download.\n\nAuthentication: Viewer or Admin via Cloudflare Access. Phase 0 returns an\nempty placeholder; Phase 1 will stream upstream content with a\n``Content-Disposition: attachment`` header.\n\nArgs:\n    document_id: Opaque document identifier sourced from the cache.\n\nReturns:\n    Response: Placeholder binary response.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "documents",
                ":document_id",
                "download"
              ],
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/documents/:document_id/download",
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "document_id",
                  "value": "example"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is in the expected range', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 422]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "name": "Inline document preview",
          "request": {
            "description": "Stream a PDF preview proxied from the ``family_office`` backend.\n\nAuthentication: Viewer or Admin via Cloudflare Access. Phase 0 returns an\nempty placeholder; Phase 1 will stream upstream content.\n\nArgs:\n    document_id: Opaque document identifier sourced from the cache.\n\nReturns:\n    Response: Placeholder PDF response.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "type": "text",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "documents",
                ":document_id",
                "preview"
              ],
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/documents/:document_id/preview",
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "document_id",
                  "value": "example"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "name": "documents"
    },
